From a6e662295885a383f8b35d724367297bd144d855 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: colum <git@volf.co>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 20:34:16 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] lanes: TF_DS_SCORE=1 scores a recorded continuation through
 the forced-window path (/v1/completions' tensorfold_score, off by default)

The quality set is undefined and nothing reports a probability: the server refuses `logprobs`
(server/fields.zig:276-284), so the `0053` expert prune and cap and EAQ v1 against v1.1 have no numeric gate, and
tools/ had no scoring harness. Baseten's `score` (crates/engine/src/bin/run.rs:253-305) prefills a prompt, feeds a
recorded continuation through the decode forward, and reports mean NLL with its standard error, perplexity and the
argmax match rate. This builds the same thing on the round the engine already runs.

A non-standard `tensorfold_score: [id, id, ...]` field on /v1/completions, with `prompt` as token ids, asks for that
instead of generating. It is refused with a 400 unless TF_DS_SCORE=1 (`1` or `on`; unset, `0`, `off` or anything else
leave it off), the engine reports api.Info.score (dsv41's `teacher_forced`: only its lanes backend copies a round's
logits to the host), n is 1 (as for every request), stream is false, temperature is 0, and the list is non-empty with
every id inside the vocabulary; on /v1/chat/completions it is refused too. With the switch off nothing else changes:
the field is refused, no other reply carries a `score` block, and the base reply is byte for byte what it was.

The engine side rides the forced-window machinery. A score stream's force list is its recorded continuation
(Stream.score, filled at Stream.init): the prompt pass pops the first token as the stream's own first, and each round's
plan takes the next five into a `Kind.forced` window whose sixth is popped at the keep, so a round feeds and scores six
recorded ids. engine.conclude already accepts every forced row whatever the target picked, so no new decision exists on
the wire: rank 1 runs the same rows from the verify frame's ids (writeWin) and the keep is rank 0's alone. A score
stream drafts nothing (drafts false: no head pass, no copy window, no graft, no held rows) and takes the family round
whatever TF_DS_GPU_TOKENS says; its rounds set sampling.RoundRules.logits, so the round takes the host_draw path and
every row's fp32 logits reach the host (m.roundLogits). The first recorded token is scored from the prompt pass's head
(m.promptLogitsHost: the row the pass draws from), and each round row records logit[recorded] - logsumexp(row) in
float64 and whether the row's argmax was the recorded token (lanes/score.zig, whose summary gives the mean, its
standard error, the perplexity and the share). The reply's `tensorfold` block gains
`score: {tokens, nll_sum, nll_mean, nll_se, ppl, argmax_match}`; `usage` and `choices` are unchanged, the reply's text
being the recorded continuation decoded.

Forcing host_draw changes how every stream in that round gets its tokens (logits copied to the host instead of the
device argmax). It should not change a greedy stream's token, and that is the thing to prove: a score request waits
for the lane (error.ContextFull, the lane host's requeue) and so starts alone, and a stream arriving later can still
share its rounds. tools/validate.py's concurrent check is the gate before that is relied on; until then PARALLEL=1
gives the solo case. Rank 1 needs nothing new, so there is no cross-rank switch agreement to compare (unlike 0051,
0054 and 0111).

tools/score.py mirrors tools/exact.py's client and record shape: `record --in set.jsonl --out base.json` scores a
JSONL set of {id, prompt_ids, continuation_ids} one item at a time and stores the reply's score block per item with
the set's digest, `compare A.json B.json` gives the paired per-item difference of the mean negative log-likelihood
with its standard error (a lossless arm must give 0), and `--self-test` checks the statistics on synthetic rows. The
sets themselves (tools/score_sets/) are not generated in this pass.

Tests: zig build test passes, including the new host tests in lanes/score.zig (a toy row's hand-computed
log-probability, the log-sum-exp staying finite where an unshifted exp overflows, a summary's mean, standard error,
perplexity and argmax share) and in engine_test.zig (a score stream's windows: five forced ids a round and a six-row
window, a short last round, a continuation of length one and no round; a score request waiting for the lane, and an
empty score list generating as ever); zig/tests/server/zig_test.sh passes, including the switch's parse and the
field's refusals and ids. Not run on a pair: no smoke, no validate.py, no benchmark. Per-token NLLs are left out of
the reply. (Patch 0120 of the series, plan item 2.)
